      "message": "fix(wire): stamp the wire contour's side by its own value and an open run's clearance\n\nThe Wire Contour arm of OpParams::stamp_with wrote the side as\n`side == Punch`, so Die, Left and Right digested alike, and never\nwrote the run-out clearance: an open run turned left <-> right, or\ngiven a new clearance, kept its stamp and its old path read Ok.\n\nThe side now writes its own discriminant - Die 0 and Punch 1, the\nbytes they always wrote, so no closed cut's stamp moves - and Left\n(2) / Right (3) follow it with the clearance, which only an open run\nreads. A closed cut's clearance still moves nothing.\n\nPinned by crates/app/tests/wire_stamp.rs: a generated open run whose\nside or clearance is re-stated in its file reads Stale; all four sides\nstamp apart; die/punch ignore the clearance; an unrelated edit and a\nplain round trip leave the cuts Ok.\n\nFixes #1370\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
